2026-10-13T23:07:29.3811924Z [pds-bl-bounded-import-unpack] MEASURED, this run, on a 50331648-byte largest member (OTP 27): unpack/1 (binary, [:memory]) peak=100859944 B = 2.0x the largest member · unpack_to_dir/2 peak=50501192 B = 1.0x. THE CLAIM IS '1x THE LARGEST MEMBER', NEVER 'CONSTANT MEMORY'. Runs of this test have measured the disk path anywhere from 0.01x to 1.01x — the spread IS the point: :erl_tar exposes no chunked EXTRACT API, so whether a given member is held whole is an implementation detail, and 1x the largest member is the bound actually owed. On guerrilla that is ~1.31 GB (mutation_events) — RE-MEASURE rather than quoting: the database grew 63.6 MB in one day.
